{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (multimodal, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) scored 0.507 acc / 0.455 F1, while config_014 (RNA-only, scgpt, transformer) scored 0.514 acc / 0.498 F1. The multimodal model underperformed the RNA-only baseline, suggesting the concat fusion may be introducing noise or misalignment from the image branch. Question: config_010 isolates a single variable—changing fusion from concat to weighted—while keeping scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, and multiprofile identical to config_005. This directly tests whether weighted fusion can rescue the multimodal setup or whether the image modality itself is unhelpful. Rationale: With 7 experiments remaining, a clean single-variable comparison is the most information-efficient next step. If weighted fusion improves over concat, it confirms fusion strategy is the bottleneck and guides subsequent experiments toward better fusion/aggregation combinations. If it still underperforms RNA-only, we can pivot decisively toward RNA-centric or alternative image-encoder configurations, saving budget."
}

